{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The stainless screws were the one close match because I recently bought several kinds of nails and wood screws, so another fastener could fit my current work.",
    "Their small size could suit a light attachment job, but I would need to confirm the length and head type before choosing them."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The hydraulic repair kit, plumbing fitting and discharge hose require specific tasks or compatible equipment that my recent purchases do not indicate.",
    "Contact cement, cutting wheels and oxalic acid relate broadly to repair work, but fastening wood does not mean I need adhesive, metal cutting or surface treatment.",
    "Replacing vacuum bags means maintaining equipment I already use; it does not give me a reason to buy another trash can."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My purchases seemed to be treated as a general interest in tools and repair supplies, although I choose supplies for particular jobs.",
    "Items that could belong in the same workshop were treated as relevant even when they serve unrelated purposes."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of framing nails and wood screws make fastening a stronger clue than a broad interest in home maintenance.",
    "Dimensions, material, head style and tool compatibility matter: even another screw is only useful if it fits the attachment I need.",
    "My medicine cups and vacuum bags reflect separate practical needs, rather than a reason to expand into unrelated equipment."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my fastening needs but stretched them into an unsupported interest in general repair equipment."
}"}
